<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n2863" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Antĭgŏnēa</span></b> ,
			ae, f., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ἀντιγόνεια</span> or <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ἀντιγονία</span>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>the name of several towns.</i>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>In Epirus</i>, <i><span class="en">Liv. 32,
			5</span></i>; <i><span class="en">43,
			23</span></i>.—Hence, <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">An-tĭgŏnensis</span></b> : 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ager,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Liv.
					43, 23</span></i>
			; and <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">An-tĭgŏnenses</span></b> , ium,
				m., <i>its inhabitants</i>, <i><span class="en">Plin. 4</span></i>,
			praef. 1, 1.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>In Macedonia</i>, <i><span class="en">Liv. 44,
			10</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>III.</b>
			<i>In Arcadia</i>, <i><span class="en">Plin. 4, 6,
				10, § 20</span></i>.— </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>IV.</b>
			<i>In Troas</i>, afterwards called <i>Alexandria</i>, <i><span class="en">Plin. 5, 30, 33, §
		124</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
    <div class="alpheios-lex-alph-source">From <u>
            <u>A Latin Dictionary</u>
        </u> (Charlton T. Lewis, Charles Short, Oxford, Clarendon Press, 1879) </div>
